Data (count: 20) passes through the forward lens's mapping (from.count, line 7
of 1.0) and violates schema 1.0's bound (<10, line 3). Only Translate finds it.

The positions are the bound and the data, never the mapping that carried the
value: the evaluator cites values, and the lens's reference is not a conjunct
where the conflict arises. A second error, from the comprehension in
translate.cue that builds the steps, adds a kernel position. Paths are
Translate's internals (Translate.out.steps._accum.1.result.count).
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
